16 December 1998	V1-1
	Initial release of the MCS.

28 January 1999		V1-2
	Fixed a datum bug.
	Used for obtaining Dedication images.

28 June 1999		V1-3
	Never used.

12 July 1999		V1-4
	Velocity feedback from PMAC working.
	Datum flag added to Az/El subsystem screens.
	Screen sizes for Az/El subsystems now the same.
	Changes to mcsInstall to accommodate new release mechanism.

24 September 1999	V1-5
	Top-level Makefile replaced with latest version from EPICS release.
	mcsInstall changed so that build output goes to screen as well as file.
	AZCONFIG/ELCONFIG changed so that a change of encoder sets the datum
	flag back to "NOT DATUMED".
	Makefile.Unix changed in src/misc to remove link dependency on -lgen.
	This prevents problems with running solaris executables under 5.6 and 5.7.
	Took out line which set encoder to FDE during a datum.
	Run AZCONFIG/ELCONFIG at startup to automatically use the tape encoders.

4 October 1999		V1-6
	Added balancing screen and records.
	Added ability to datum with tape heads (still needs debugging).
	Added accurate time-stamping of position and velocity for TCS.
	Added automatic version number to top-level screen.

19 October 1999		V1-7
	Implemented RELOAD and INIT commands.
	Removed READLUT and UNWRAP stubs.
	General tidying up.

01 November 1999	V1-8
	Added extra diagnostics for Datum with tape encoders.
	Changed DPRAM memory location for Motion Program Handshake bit.
	Added DPRAM memory location for time-stamping strobe bit (so
	that ASCII mailboxes are not being used at 10Hz).
	Implemented averaging over 10 seconds for elevation torque feedback.

03 December 1999	V1-9
	Implemented and tested datum for both azimuth and elevation tape encoders.

29 June 2001    	V2-0
	Implemented and tested:
       
        - "Double buffer" follow.
        - Busy/Idle transition.
        - Close Loop after a datum using sony switch.

29 June 2001    	V2-2
	Debug of PMAC logging. implemented automatic log file translation.


20 August 2001    	V2-3
	PMAC simulator implemented. 

20 September 2001       V2-4
        Ported to EPICS3.13.4GEM7.

        Implemented and tested:

        - New Health tree with informative Messages.
          This Health tree includes the Time bus health
          and status of data stream from TCS.

        - Time stamped az/el positions.

30 September 2002    	V2-6

        - Ported to PPC board. 
   
        - new timeStamp.

        - NO trajectory calculation YET.

29 November 2003        V3-0

	- Trajectory Calculation Implemented.
        
	- Inposition calculation bug fixed.

25 August 2008 			V3-3
	- Extra protection for follow trigger. Pmac
	variable P102 set to 0 when MCS is not in follow mode.

7 May 2010	V3-4
	- logTRacking command added.
	- Added debug capabilities to the move and follow commands.
	- added log_console command.

16 March 2015   V3-5
        - BFOSW 27
        - Assert/Disassert will be enabled (using SDIS) whenever timer is on or we are in Base Mode.
        - Corresponding EPICS DM screens (mcs-ws.rpm) will display TSRS Mode and enable bit (from timer)
          on Alt and AZ screens where assert/dissassert is controlled. 

24 June 2016    V3-6
	Attempt to get MCS working in simulation mode. Only partially succesfull.  At least got  the system 
	to simulates the drive condition response from the GIS which helped developing REL-2548
	
	files changed: 
	M capfast/pmacMotor1servo.sch   new revision: 1.2
	M capfast/pmacMotorStat1.sch	new revision: 1.5
	M capfast/pmacSimulator.sch	new revision: 1.2
	M capfast/setPositions.sch	new revision: 1.4
	M capfast/simulate.sch		new revision: 1.3
	M src/misc/datum.c		new revision: 1.12
	M src/misc/simRoutines.c	new revision: 1.3
	A startup/startupSim.vws	initial revision: 1.1

	REL-2548 Improve MCS Drive Assert Sequencing.
	Change the Move, Datum and Follow drive assert sequencing to continue immediately after the DriveCondition changes.
        The old 12 second timeout is retained and will handle the case where the GIS fails to set driveCondition

        files changed:
	M capfast/GISassert.sch		new revision: 1.2
	M capfast/gisAxis.sch		new revision: 1.5


